  "observationBoundary": "One BizHawk 2.11.1 / Genesis Plus GX launch enters the original CheckSram call, redirects only its post-return continuation through a work-RAM checkpoint, saves one core state outside input/memory callbacks, and replays four SRAM-flag/menu-result cases. The observer uses session-only MD CART patches after recording M68K BUS and MD CART readback for each patched word; it bypasses both ExecuteWitchMainMenu calls, j_NameAlly, and DisplayText, pulses C only to release text-macro waits after witchMenuAction_New entry, and clears PLAYER_1_INPUT before the original CheatModeConfiguration early-return check. It executes the original witchMenuAction_New, j_NewGame/NewGame, difficulty flag code, SaveGame, and MainLoop handoff. It does not establish player-driven menu or naming input, pixels, audio, text cadence, cross-process SRAM persistence, or power-loss behavior.",
